  "timingConditions": "Same foreground phone, low quality and original game rules. Idle windows are approximately 6.5 seconds at spawn with four rotating cones. Each active window uses six alternating pairs of 180ms left/right primary holds and 330ms releases while ball motion and automatic jumps remain enabled. No game-state writes. Browser HUD and Android HUD use different rendering resolutions. Timing covers app-frame to app-frame and/or display presentation as identified per series. No GPU timer or power measurement.",
  "limits": [
    "One device, one short level; no median across devices or long-run thermal claim.",
    "The native HUD uses a local bitmap font instead of the browser text rasterizer. Its contrast, score progression, victory and replay behavior are checked. Pixel-identical character outlines are outside this measurement.",
    "The native game includes three-dimensional primitives, its original collisions and camera tracking, and shared 2D HUD. Arbitrary World3D materials, effects or models are not covered."
  ]
